    "title": "Where to watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball in FIBA World Cup Qualifiers. Schedule, time, stats",
    "text": "Updated March 14, 2026, 2:04 p.m. ETCaitlin Clark is playing for USA Basketball in the FIBA World Cup Qualifying Tournament in Puerto Rico.Clark is returning to the court after an eight-month absence due to multiple injuries.The team's next game is against Italy on Saturday, March 14, 2026.SAN JUAN, PUERTO RICO — Indiana Fever star Caitlin Clark did not have the same success in her second game of the FIBA World Cup Qualifying Tournament this week, and understandably so.Clark, 24, was playing the second game of a back-to-back having not played one game in eight months after recovering from a multitude of injuries that ended her sophomore WNBA season.Her first game was a triumphant return. She had 17 points and 12 assists to two turnovers in USA Basketball's 110-46 win over Senegal on Wednesday night.The U.S. has already qualified for the World Cup, set for September in Berlin, Germany, but it is competing in order to get extra reps for younger players on the national team. That was apparent Thursday night, a 91-48 win over Puerto Rico. Clark had eight points, three rebounds and two assists as lineups looked disjointed at times.Here's how to watch Clark and USA Basketball in their qualifiers.Where to watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball vs. Italy today, Saturday, March 14, 2026USA Basketball will tip off against Italy at 5 p.m. Saturday, March 14. It will air on TruTV/HBO Max. This will be the first game between USA and Italy since 1979.Watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball on Sling!Does Caitlin Clark play today? Caitlin Clark plays in USA vs Italy women's basketball game today Saturday, March 14, 2026Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball play Game 3 against Italy at 5 p.m. Saturday, March 14.Buy Caitlin Clark gear on Fanatics!What time does Caitlin Clark play today? When does USA Basketball play Italy in FIBA World Cup qualifier today, Saturday, March 14, 2026?Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball return to action today against Italy at 5 p.m., Saturday, March 14.Where is USA Basketball, Caitlin Clark playing in the 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiers?The tournament is being hosted in San Juan, Puerto Rico.When is Caitlin Clark's next game? When is the next USA Basketball game in 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiers?After Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball's third game, they return to action Sunday, March 15, 2026, against New Zealand at 2 p.m.Buy Caitlin Clark's Nike merch!Caitlin Clark points, stats, in USA Basketball games at 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiersIn 19 minutes, Caitlin Clark scored 17 points with 12 assists to two turnovers in a tournament-opening 110-46 win over Senegal on Wednesday. Read more here.Clark's offense was not as effective in her second game, that in as many days after eight months recovering from an injury. She finished with eight points, three rebounds and two assists in the 91-48 win over Puerto Rico on Thursday. Read more here.USA Basketball results at 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifying tournamentWednesday, March 11: USA 110, Senegal 46. INSIDERThursday, March 12: USA 91, Puerto Rico 48. INSIDERUSA Basketball schedule in 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifying tournamentHere is the full schedule (all times ET):Saturday, March 14: vs Italy, 5 p.m.Sunday, March 15: vs New Zealand, 2 p.m.Tuesday, March 17: vs Spain, 5 p.m.Watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball live!Chloe Peterson is the Indiana Fever beat reporter for IndyStar. Reach her at capeterson@gannett.com or follow her on X at @chloepeterson67.Get IndyStar's Indiana Fever and Caitlin Clark coverage sent directly to your inbox with our Caitlin Clark Fever newsletter. Subscribe to IndyStar's YouTube channel for Fever Insiders Live.",
